            {
              "message": "project: bound the speaker index a transcript word may carry (#4140)\n\nTranscript::normalize sized the speaker label table from the largest word\nspeaker index, so one word with a u32::MAX index made transcript.set allocate\nbillions of labels before check() could run. Indices at or past MAX_SPEAKERS\n(1024) now lose their speaker instead.",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/filmcraft/commit/57dc82ea2046c2ec479ab4d4d8167d90e5500b49",
              "date": "2026-11-03T11:02:57Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "edit: look up higher-track transcript coverage by binary search (#4123)",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/filmcraft/commit/b37811ec534727fe0d451f89656a407a846d50a9",
              "date": "2026-11-03T11:02:49Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "dng: budget SubIFD references before reading and queueing them (#4108)",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/filmcraft/commit/3a2ef6fe90048b692c339714368d2b4c292522c2",
              "date": "2026-11-03T11:02:41Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "macOS: keep AppKit's Touch Bar observers when AccessKit drops (no crash on quit) (#4002)\n\n* macOS: keep AppKit's Touch Bar observers when AccessKit drops (no crash on quit)\n\naccesskit_macos 0.27.1 reset the window's view to WinitView when its adapter\ndropped, discarding the key-value observation AppKit's Touch Bar finder had put\non the view's nextResponder. On quit, AppKit's removal of that observer raised\nand _crashOnException: ended FilmCraft with SIGILL on Touch Bar Macs. 0.27.2\nresets the class only while it is still AccessKit's own subclass.\n\nLockfile-only bump (accesskit 0.25.2, accesskit_consumer 0.39.2, accesskit_macos\n0.27.2), with a test that fails below 0.27.2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D5nRpBjuSq2YBDMKU2Spqs\n\n* filmcraft: accesskit lock test in the it binary; leave tempfile's getrandom as it was\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Thomas <echelon@gmail.com>",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/filmcraft/commit/32749e34f611735460e9773335345db026b7b037",
              "date": "2026-11-03T05:10:12Z"
            },
            {
              "message": "fix(timeline): the Mix row's level sets the Mix fader (#3765) (#3954)\n\n* fix(timeline): the Mix row's level sets the Mix fader (#3765)\n\nThe Timeline's Mix track header painted the master level as hot text but\nnothing could change it, so the Mix volume seemed to do nothing. It is now a\nhot number, as on an audio track: drag or type to set the Mix fader. It\nshows the fader at the playhead (its automation, or a control held in the\nAudio Track Mixer) and changes it through mixer.setValue, which writes a\nkeyframe where the Mix fader is automated.\n\nmixer.setValue takes `merge` / `begin`, as clipMixer.set does, so a drag\nis one undo step; a typed value is its own. Without `merge` nothing changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mixer): a merged Mix drag stays in its own sequence (#3765)\n\nThe Mix strip has the same id in every sequence, so the merge key of\nmixer.setValue now names the active sequence too. Otherwise one undo\ncould revert Mix drags in two sequences.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(timeline): drag the Mix level as a held gesture (#3765)\n\nDuring playback an automation pass runs, and mixer.setValue touches and\nreleases the control on every call, so each drag update of the Timeline's\nMix level was its own undo step (and in Touch the return started from the\nlast update). The field now does what the Audio Track Mixer's fader does:\nmixer.touch while dragging and mixer.release when the drag ends; a typed\nvalue still goes through mixer.setValue. Outside playback the release\ncommits the value once, so the merge/begin params of mixer.setValue are\nno longer needed and are removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(timeline): the Touch return starts at the Mix drag's release (#3765)\n\nThe drag test helper calls `between` once more before the release, so the\nplayhead moves after the last drag update; the Touch test checks that the\nkeyframe at the release time holds the released value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* timeline: empty_state keeps its doc comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Thomas <echelon@gmail.com>",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/filmcraft/commit/19fb3366cedd830d229bb197fc35472ec7b77a1e",
              "date": "2026-11-03T05:10:07Z"
            }
